# Track worktrees are separate checkouts living inside the repo. They are excluded
# from git via .git/info/exclude, but prettier walks them anyway — so a local
# `format:check` fails on another track's in-progress scratch files while a build
# loop is running, and walking ~25GB of sibling checkouts takes minutes rather
# than seconds. CI never sees them (they are not in any commit).
#
# THIS LINE GOVERNS THE REPO-ROOT WALK ONLY, and that distinction is load-bearing.
# Prettier applies an ignore file to explicitly-named paths exactly as it does to
# walked ones, so while the format hook ran from the repo root this line also made
# it silently skip every file an agent wrote inside a worktree: `prettier --write
# <path-in-worktree>` exited 0, printed nothing, and changed nothing. Unformatted
# code then reached CI, which is the only formatter check that could still see it
# (a CI fail on #302).
#
# The fix is in `.claude/settings.json` (PostToolUse) and `.cursor/hooks/format.sh`
# (afterFileEdit): each hook resolves the NEAREST `.prettierignore` walking up
# from the file it was handed and passes it as `--ignore-path`. For a file in the
# main checkout that is this file, unchanged. For a file inside a worktree it is
# that worktree's own copy, where the patterns resolve against the worktree root
# — so `node_modules`/`.next` still apply and the line below does not match
# `src/...`. Do not "simplify" that flag away, and do not delete this line:
# dropping it makes `pnpm format:check` walk every sibling worktree.
.claude/worktrees/

